{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeL6yJ6GmuXp2P9zpwcfj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015rNzseAcLHZtpBt5itNwDM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ammarbinayaz/.claude/plans/cross-layer-feature-build-virtual-raccoon.md","content":"# T5 review queue — pre-implementation plan review\n\nReviewed against `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-queue.test.mjs` (frozen, read-only)\nand the task contract. No files were modified.\n\n## Blocking gaps\n\n1. **`createReviewApi` return type is under-specified.** The visible suite does\n   `const handle = createReviewApi(store); handle({ ... })`. The plan says \"Return\n   `handleReviewRequest(request)`\", which a worker can read as returning\n   `{ handleReviewRequest }`. It must return the bare function.\n2. **Exact review object shape.** `assert.deepEqual(created.body.review, { runId, decision,\n   reviewer, note, createdAt, updatedAt })` fails on any extra key. The plan never forbids\n   added fields (`id`, `version`, `history`, `status`). Store and API must emit exactly six keys.\n3. **Page markup literals are not pinned.** `/<main>/` requires a bare `<main>` tag — `<main\n   id=\"content\">` or `<main\\n>` fails. `<label for=\"run-id\">Run ID</label>` is matched verbatim,\n   so the control is `id=\"run-id\"` with `name=\"runId\"`; the plan's \"matching `for`/`id` pairs and\n   correct `name` attributes\" does not state that ids and names differ. `<caption>Saved run\n   reviews</caption>`, `aria-live=\"polite\"`, and `No reviews yet.` are also exact.\n4. **Timestamp ordering must be string comparison.** `now` is only contracted to return a\n   non-empty string. Any `new Date(...)` / `Date.parse` sort key yields `NaN` for a non-ISO clock\n   and silently breaks `list` ordering. Compare `updatedAt` with `<`/`>` on strings.\n5. **`now` call ordering.** The clock helper is positional, so a save that throws after calling\n   `now` desynchronizes every later timestamp. Validate the whole input first, then call `now`\n   exactly once, then reject a non-string/empty result with `TypeError`.\n6. **Absent POST fields are unspecified.** The plan only covers \"non-string value is a field\n   error\", which silently makes an omitted `note` a 400 on an `approve`. Needs an explicit,\n   documented rule.\n7. **`fields` value type is unspecified**, so `fields.body` (sorted unknown names) may end up an\n   array while other entries are strings. Pin one type.\n\n## Corrected contract decisions\n\n- `createReviewApi(store)` returns the `handleReviewRequest` function itself; optionally attach\n  `fn.handleReviewRequest = fn` for tolerance. Throw `TypeError` when `store` is not an object or\n  any of `save`/`get`/`list` is not callable.\n- Reviews carry exactly `runId, decision, reviewer, note, createdAt, updatedAt`. `save` returns\n  `{ created, review }` with a fresh shallow copy; `get` returns a copy or `null` (never throws,\n  including for a non-string `runId`); `list` returns a new array of new copies.\n- `save` validation order: reject non-object/array/`null` input and any non-string among the four\n  fields with `TypeError` → call `now()` once → reject non-string or empty timestamp with\n  `TypeError` → insert (`createdAt === updatedAt`) or update (keep `createdAt`).\n- `list` sorts by `updatedAt` descending as strings, ties by `runId` ascending; `decision` filter\n  is exact equality.\n- Every `fields` entry is a non-empty human-readable string. `fields.body` is a single string\n  embedding the sorted unknown names (e.g. `Unknown fields: alpha, zeta`). The visible suite only\n  inspects `Object.keys(fields).sort()`.\n- Missing/`undefined` `note` normalizes to `\"\"` before validation (it is then rejected for\n  `reject`/`needs-work` by the required-note rule); missing/`undefined` `runId`, `decision`, and\n  `reviewer` are per-field errors. Any non-string, non-`undefined` value (`null`, number, object)\n  is a per-field error for all four fields and is never trimmed. Document this in the README.\n- A `body` that is not a plain object (missing, `null`, array, string, primitive) is\n  `validation_failed` with a `body` field error. Do not `JSON.parse` string bodies; note in the\n  README that the boundary takes already-parsed JSON.\n- Routing: normalize `method` with `toUpperCase()`; parse against a fixed base\n  (`new URL(url, \"http://localhost\")`); strip one trailing slash, so `/api/reviews/` is the\n  collection. `/api/reviews` → `GET, POST`; `/api/reviews/<one-segment>` → `GET`; anything deeper\n  or different → 404 `not_found` regardless of method. 405 responses carry both `allow` and the\n  JSON content type.\n- `invalid_request` (400) covers a non-object request, non-string `method` or `url`, a throwing\n  `URL` constructor, and a `decodeURIComponent` failure on the detail segment. Scope that\n  `try/catch` to request parsing only — do not wrap `store` calls.\n- `GET /api/reviews`: call `store.list()` once unfiltered, build `summary` from it, then filter\n  `reviews` in the API so both stay consistent. `summary` has exactly `total`, `approve`,\n  `reject`, `\"needs-work\"`. A `decision` query is trimmed then exact-matched; absent → no filter;\n  present-but-invalid (including empty) → standard validation error. Ignore other query params.\n- `renderReviewPage` tolerates `renderReviewPage()` and missing keys: `reviews = []`,\n  `summary = {}` rendering `0` for absent counts, `message = \"\"`. Escape via\n  `value == null ? \"\" : String(value)` then replace `&`, `<`, `>`, `\"`, `'` with `&` first.\n  Dynamic values go only into text nodes, never into attributes or tag names.\n\n## Worker checklist\n\n1. `review-store.mjs` per the ordering and copy rules above.\n2. `review-api.mjs`: single-pass validation collecting all field errors, never calling `save` when\n   any error exists; 201 insert / 200 update.\n3. `review-page.mjs`: reproduce the five literal fragments exactly; four labeled controls\n   (`run-id`/`runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, `note`), decision `select` with the three values,\n   note-required help text, `aria-live=\"polite\"` status region, table with caption, five columns,\n   and the empty-state row.\n4. `student-tests.mjs` — at least four cases, none duplicating the visible four, no skip/todo:\n   (a) store: tie-break sort, returned-value mutation cannot alter state, `now` called exactly\n   once per save (counter), non-string `now` result throws `TypeError`;\n   (b) API: aggregated errors with sorted unknown fields plus trimming, and `store.list()` still\n   empty;\n   (c) API: filtered `reviews` with unfiltered `summary`, update returns 200 and preserves\n   `createdAt`, 404 detail, 404 unknown route, 405 `allow` plus content-type, `invalid_request`;\n   (d) page: inject `\"><script>` through `message`, a summary value, and all five review fields;\n   assert escaped text present and raw markup absent.\n5. `README.md`: three routes, field rules and trimming, create/update statuses, filter vs summary,\n   all error bodies including `allow`, JSON content type, the documented missing-`note` rule, and\n   an explicit warning that the store is in-memory and resets on process restart.\n6. Verify with the exact command, then `git status --short` and `git diff --check`. Touch only the\n   five owned files; report only visible results.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":16292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3a274a2-c45f-4d4c-8f2e-cd63e431b3cd","uuid":"119376b9-c945-4879-a5ef-1543459876ff","timestamp":"2026-08-23T17:52:30.897Z","request_id":"req_011CeL6yH7V1FBySnKtpET